sweep:
I rendered both levels with a marker at every key opening (L1_marked.png, L2_marked.png and eight final_*.png tiles with the final keys) and checked by geometry:

(1) Door blocks: all 40 A-DOOR inserts match a key opening within 1 mm of its centre; the two pivot panels share B1-08. Every A-DOOR line and arc belongs to a door block except the cabinet doors of the L2 IA_J12_CABINET (casework). No swing, leaf or block is missing from the keys.

(2) Wall gaps: I searched the hatch-filled wall mass (A-WALL plus A-WALL-PATT fills, columns, glass), casting a ray up to 4 m from every free wall end. It finds every key gap. Everything else it finds is not an opening:
- the closed void under the lift shaft (both levels);
- the 0.58 m slot in the L1 east wall, filled by the through-wall ATM (equipment);
- the cavities and linings of the double-leaf facades;
- the toilet-lobby back-wall ends inside the L2 toilets;
- the 2.98 m open front of the FOR 1 PAX nook;
- the stub left by the B2-07 clash.

(3) Ends: all 41 key openings meet solid within 2 mm of a and b. The glass-partition doors (B1-07, B1-10 to B1-12) include their 25 mm jamb mullions and the curtain-wall doors (B1-08, B1-09) their 50 mm mullions, as the key's frame-included rule says.

No key entry is wrong; corrections: none. B2-07 stays at the 1.000 m frame both labellers chose. The female toilet's south wall crosses its top 0.125 m, which is a drawing clash; the clear wall gap would be 0.875, and the entry already notes this.

Additions, all on L1 and all optional, so the scored counts stay at 16 and 25:
- B1-91 to B1-98: the 8 curtain-wall glazed panels that sit in gaps of the facade wall line between wall ends and columns (verified: solid at both ends, fully glazed between). Both labellers listed them as glass walls. Under the 26 Oct definition they read as windows, the plan cannot settle it, and a detector reading A-WALL gaps will report them.
- B1-99: the passage mouth where the corridor north of the meeting room opens into the stair / ATM hall. The free end of the toilet's east wall faces the meeting-room wall 1.08 m away.

The interior GLASS WALL partitions stay glass walls: on L1 the manager room, meeting room and lobby screens, on L2 the wealth room. They are partitions made of glass, and a reader of wall layers sees no gap there because they sit on A-WALL. Level 2 has no additions.

Final keys: L1 has 25 entries (16 scored, 9 optional); L2 has 25, unchanged.
